regions={'chest':'pectoralis major','deltoids':'deltoid muscles','upper-back':'latissimus dorsi and upper back','trapezius':'trapezius','serratus':'serratus anterior','biceps':'biceps brachii','triceps':'triceps brachii','forearm':'forearm muscles','abs':'rectus abdominis','obliques':'external and internal obliques','lower-back':'spinal erectors','gluteal':'gluteal muscles','quadriceps':'quadriceps','hamstring':'hamstrings','adductors':'hip adductors','hip-flexors':'hip flexors','calves':'gastrocnemius and soleus','tibialis':'tibialis anterior'}
jobs=[]
for a in actions:
    if (a.get('media') or {}).get('path'):continue
    ident=a['exerciseKey'].removeprefix('opengym-')
    if ident not in hints:raise SystemExit('Missing motion specification: '+ident)
    primary=', '.join(regions.get(m,m) for m in a['primaryMuscles'])
    secondary=', '.join(regions.get(m,m) for m in a['secondaryMuscles'])
    prompt=f'''Use case: scientific-educational. One instructional ANIMATION KEYFRAME SPRITE SHEET for {a['englishName']}.
Output exactly FOUR columns and TWO rows, eight equal SQUARE tiles, overall aspect ratio 2:1. Uniform grid without borders, gutters, numbers, captions or labels. Each tile contains ONE phase of the SAME exercise, row-major time sequence. This sheet will be cropped into eight frames and its exact reverse will form the return movement.
References: Image 1 specifies our APPROVED anatomical illustration style; Image 2 supports the same muscle-rendering and equipment style. Do not copy the reference push-up or bench pose: draw the requested exercise below.
Style: pure white background; finely shaded GRAYSCALE anatomical adult man, short dark hair, BLACK shorts, visible clean muscle contours, no gore. Equipment neutral gray/black. Main trained muscles ({primary}) muted deep red; secondary muscles ({secondary or 'none'}) lighter coral. Accurate local muscle patches only, stable colors in every tile, no glowing whole-body regions or flashing. Preserve the approved thin linework, proportions and soft shadows.
Motion specification: {hints[ident]}
For a dynamic exercise: frame 1 is the described START, frame 8 the described END; six smooth incremental positions in between. For an ISOMETRIC HOLD: hold the correct position in ALL frames and show ONLY extremely subtle breathing; never invent repetitions. For a unilateral example, demonstrate ONE side consistently, not a different side in each tile.
Camera: fixed clear three-quarter view chosen to make the required limb motion, equipment and muscle regions visible. Same camera, lighting, equipment, body proportions, frame origin and scale in all eight tiles. Entire body, all weights and support/anchor apparatus visible with comfortable margins in every tile. Realistic gravity and mechanically connected equipment. All planted hands, feet, support contacts and anchors stay at exactly the same positions relative to their tile. Only the exercise's actual joints move; neutral neck and spine as specified. Natural controlled range, no distorted hands, extra limbs or intersecting equipment. Do not change grip type, exercise variant, band connection, bench angle or number of weights across frames. This is one coherent motion, not eight unrelated views.'''
    job={'id':'remaining-'+ident,'exerciseKey':a['exerciseKey'],'name':a['displayName'],'englishName':a['englishName'],'primaryMuscles':a['primaryMuscles'],'secondaryMuscles':a['secondaryMuscles'],'recordingMode':a['recordingMode'],'laterality':a['laterality'],'prompt':prompt,'motionSpec':hints[ident],'status':'not_generated'}
    jobs.append(job)
    (folder/(job['id']+'-prompt.txt')).write_bytes((prompt+'\n').encode('utf-8'))
existing_path=folder/'jobs.json'
if existing_path.exists():
    old={j['id']:j for j in json.loads(existing_path.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))}
    for job in jobs:
        if old.get(job['id'],{}).get('status')!='not_generated':job.update(old[job['id']])
existing_path.write_bytes((json.dumps(jobs,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n').encode('utf-8'))
print(json.dumps({'jobs':len(jobs),'folder':str(folder)},ensure_ascii=False))
